"All six samples are dominated by mottled gray sky within a circular fisheye boundary. Long black curved propeller traces extend from the left across the central sky; a rounded dark blue-gray aircraft housing occupies the upper-right perimeter, while light gray supports and smaller dark fittings appear at the outer edges. Trees and narrow fragments of the roadside wrap around the perimeter, with a tiny blue sign near the top and slender lamp silhouettes around the rim. These edge fragments are distorted and partly inverted. From 0-4 seconds, the housing remains anchored to the camera while the blade traces vary in curvature, position and apparent spacing; the peripheral landscape shifts subtly with aircraft attitude. The final sample at 4.9375 seconds shows another small peripheral shift and continued blade-trace variation, with the housing still at upper right. Multiple traces cannot establish an exact rotor count. No pedestrian, readable sign text or identifiable water surface is visible. The sky shows no clearly resolved source snowfall. The final frame is displayed until 5.0 seconds, and trailing black contact-sheet cells are padding rather than video content."
